{"data":[{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112798952055795712"]},"author_id":"733647469305864195","created_at":"2026-10-21T06:52:05.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112799064479941088"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/HKMDxkyM5w","end":298,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2112799064479941088/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112798952055795712","start":275,"url":"https://t.co/HKMDxkyM5w"},{"display_url":"x.com/PIIE/status/21…","end":322,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/PIIE/status/2112586397173309515","start":299,"url":"https://t.co/p8krPY6Njm"}]},"id":"2112799064479941088","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":24,"impression_count":8969,"like_count":66,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":3,"retweet_count":9},"text":"I agree with Nicholas Lardy that the root cause of China's surplus is still high savings (sustained by policy) relative to a reduced level of investment after the property bubble burst.\n\nBut the rise in current account surplus started well before 2024, it has just masked by https://t.co/HKMDxkyM5w https://t.co/p8krPY6Njm","url":"https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2112799064479941088"},{"author_id":"2220183580","created_at":"2026-10-21T05:59:03.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112785717373927811"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/ft/status/2112…","end":301,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/ft/status/2112743433924116942","start":278,"url":"https://t.co/dqieerGKM5"}]},"id":"2112785717373927811","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":26,"impression_count":9025,"like_count":114,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":11,"retweet_count":16},"text":"And well it might be. The parallels are striking, the dissimilarities equally so. Yet, all things considered, one of the things that maps so well is the vested interests of rigid institutions that couldn’t or wouldn’t adapt or mitigate. This, I think, is why China is the Japan https://t.co/dqieerGKM5","url":"https://x.com/georgemagnus1/status/2112785717373927811"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112782690210500608"]},"author_id":"917683048782503937","created_at":"2026-10-21T05:57:46.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112785396765474998"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/kNp1Tab6xm","end":302,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2112785396765474998/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112782690210500608","start":279,"url":"https://t.co/kNp1Tab6xm"}]},"id":"2112785396765474998","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":57,"impression_count":10881,"like_count":110,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":3,"retweet_count":17},"text":"I just finished Yoichi Funabashi's very detailed history of the events and negotiations surrounding the Plaza Accord and the subsequent Louvre Accord. What is especially interesting is that this was published in 1988, at the peak of the Japanese economic boom and at a time when https://t.co/kNp1Tab6xm","url":"https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2112785396765474998"},{"author_id":"733647469305864195","created_at":"2026-10-21T05:21:16.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112776211013534007"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/FT/status/2112…","end":236,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/FT/status/2112743433924116942","start":213,"url":"https://t.co/Zus9WyCZc8"}]},"id":"2112776211013534007","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":302,"impression_count":94975,"like_count":1024,"quote_count":11,"reply_count":63,"retweet_count":111},"text":"If China didn't want to the risk becoming the next Japan it should have done much more to promote consumption and lower savings 15 years ago -- and not allowed its property bubble to inflate for 10 years ...\n\n1/2 https://t.co/Zus9WyCZc8","url":"https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2112776211013534007"},{"author_id":"733647469305864195","created_at":"2026-10-21T05:15:49.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112774835994755329"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/michaelxpettis…","end":176,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/michaelxpettis/status/2112766917307965806","start":153,"url":"https://t.co/FpyHi5Q4oO"}]},"id":"2112774835994755329","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":1,"impression_count":6213,"like_count":20,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"32K exports (per the EU data) of hybrids and plug in hybrids last september --\n\n3x is 95-100K, or in line with the 90K pace in the EU's August data .... https://t.co/FpyHi5Q4oO","url":"https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2112774835994755329"},{"author_id":"917683048782503937","created_at":"2026-10-21T05:00:09.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112770893500064000"],"entities":{"urls":[{"description":"US and Mexican trade negotiators have hit an impasse over tariffs on steel and aluminum, dashing earlier optimism for an imminent deal and likely kicking major progress until after the midterm elections, people familiar with the matter said.","display_url":"bloomberg.com/news/articles/…","end":224,"expanded_url":"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-20/us-mexico-trade-talks-hit-impasse-as-lutnick-exerts-influence?utm_source=website&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=twitter","images":[{"height":800,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112770895303565312/sx0ZoTay?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1200},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112770895303565312/sx0ZoTay?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":201,"status":200,"title":"US-Mexico Trade Talks Hit Impasse as Lutnick Exerts Influence","unwound_url":"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-20/us-mexico-trade-talks-hit-impasse-as-lutnick-exerts-influence?utm_source=website&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=twitter","url":"https://t.co/xzW664j4ta"}]},"id":"2112770893500064000","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":19,"impression_count":11651,"like_count":147,"quote_count":5,"reply_count":7,"retweet_count":22},"text":"No one that I have spoken to on either the US side or the Mexican side seems to think that Lutnick is able to play much of a constructive role. I don't think he understands trade as an economic issue.\nhttps://t.co/xzW664j4ta","url":"https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2112770893500064000"},{"author_id":"917683048782503937","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:44:21.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112766917307965806"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":247,"id":"23922797","start":238,"username":"SCMPNews"}],"urls":[{"description":"Exports climbed to nearly 100,000 vehicles in September ahead of limits due to take effect at the end of the year.","display_url":"sc.mp/my9nm?utm_sour…","end":233,"expanded_url":"https://sc.mp/my9nm?utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=3371541&utm_medium=share_widget","images":[{"height":630,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112556604839374848/MKB4ryZT?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1200},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112556604839374848/MKB4ryZT?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":210,"title":"China’s hybrid car exports to EU surge by more than 200% as import cap looms","unwound_url":"https://www.scmp.com/economy/global-economy/article/3371541/chinas-hybrid-car-exports-eu-surge-more-200-import-cap-looms?utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=3371541&utm_medium=share_widget","url":"https://t.co/DELZNO51pS"}]},"id":"2112766917307965806","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":6,"impression_count":12258,"like_count":42,"quote_count":2,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":1},"text":"SCMP: \"China’s hybrid car exports to the European Union tripled in September from a year earlier, with shipments expected to remain elevated before an import cap agreed during recent trade talks takes effect.\"\nhttps://t.co/DELZNO51pS via @scmpnews","url":"https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2112766917307965806"},{"author_id":"733647469305864195","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:37:23.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112765167373341180"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/michaelxpettis…","end":144,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/michaelxpettis/status/2112764480635511210","start":121,"url":"https://t.co/Ky9slUXJDS"}]},"id":"2112765167373341180","public_metr